Here's the rewritten hero paragraph, same tone:

```html
                    <div style="
                          margin-top: 24px;
                          font-size: 17px;
                          line-height: 28px;
                          color: #4b5563;
                          max-width: 460px;
                        ">
                      Want a free cleaning? Shift is now offering free, professional cleaning services across NYC. Starting today, you can book a vetted cleaner at no cost and have them come right to your door.
                    </div>
```

Drop that in place of the current "Shift is bringing free, professional home cleanings..." block. Kept it casual, no em dashes, leading with the hook and closing on the concrete action (book, no cost, at your door).

```html
                    <div style="
                          margin-top: 24px;
                          font-size: 17px;
                          line-height: 28px;
                          color: #4b5563;
                          max-width: 460px;
                        ">
                      Want a <strong style="color: #111111;">free cleaning?</strong> Shift is now offering <strong style="color: #111111;">free, professional cleaning services across NYC.</strong> Starting <strong style="color: #111111;">today</strong>, you can book a vetted cleaner at <strong style="color: #111111;">no cost</strong> and have them come right to your door.
                    </div>
```

Bolded the key hooks (free cleaning, free professional cleaning services across NYC, today, no cost) in black so they pop against the gray body.

```html
                    <div style="
                          margin-top: 24px;
                          font-size: 17px;
